 coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x-2\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $-2$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141522/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec6076ff-1538-5bc0-973d-33d908b0b4d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141522"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141536/selection/2adc2b8603cb6ecc1c52507ca93e25fe8b868d964cfb6b4e4d1ea62ede6cd1d2" :answer/id #uuid "77fde76a-bf47-5c74-a85b-61db61c392b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{49}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141536/selection/5b64297173957cdb1eb5d36cd9817ec1e5f09ea1d58764c7a8bd3ae295d5d49e" :answer/id #uuid "539a3a96-4f8e-57f7-a4bd-cd62ae2ce738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{7}{4})}^{2}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141536/selection/7090b726c71a788e4141240de6612e9c1166400efe6a250d581150ccd12a4348" :answer/id #uuid "2d75f99e-41d1-5ac1-84e7-c8070067cbc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141536/selection/02267073f7fe92797eb430cb6be8dba05714544e3a7d6325f1ac123bd809ee51" :answer/id #uuid "21a26751-478f-5f29-a850-e2f7b1b6a1cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(y+\\frac{7}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141536/selection/b371f8122c5890ee4936abbe9a28d4167e1c209cb5ca57787269004eb956cf13" :answer/id #uuid "cbae702a-fe